<title>USA: Citicorp sees Mexico peso at 8.25/dlr by yearend.</title>
<headline>Citicorp sees Mexico peso at 8.25/dlr by yearend.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citicorp Securities has strengthed its end-1997 peso forecast to 8.25 per dollar from 8.46 per dollar, according to Joe Petry, the firm's chief Latin America economist.</p>
<p>Petry said Citicorp altered its outlook because of &quot;impressive election-related currency strength,&quot; strong inflows into Mexican equity markets, declining inflation and lower international interest rates.</p>
<p>(( -- Emerging Markets Unit, 212-859-1868 ))</p>
